{"fts":"ftgl https://github.com/frankheckenbach/ftgl   ftgl is a free open source library to enable developers to use arbitrary fonts in their opengl (www.opengl.org) applications. unlike other opengl font libraries ftgl uses standard font file formats so doesn't need a preprocessing step to convert the high quality font data into a lesser quality, proprietary format. ftgl uses the freetype (www.freetype.org) font library to open and 'decode' the fonts. it then takes that output and stores it in a format most efficient for opengl rendering.","name":"ftgl","version":"2.4.0","port-version":7,"description":["FTGL is a free open source library to enable developers to use arbitrary fonts in their OpenGL (www.opengl.org) applications.","Unlike other OpenGL font libraries FTGL uses standard font file formats so doesn't need a preprocessing step to convert the high quality font data into a lesser quality, proprietary format.","FTGL uses the Freetype (www.freetype.org) font library to open and 'decode' the fonts. It then takes that output and stores it in a format most efficient for OpenGL rendering."],"homepage":"https://github.com/frankheckenbach/ftgl","license":"MIT","dependencies":[{"name":"freetype","default-features":false},"opengl",{"name":"vcpkg-cmake","host":true},{"name":"vcpkg-cmake-config","host":true}],"_id":"NUzBEEN2URCf7Hqd"}
